      "writtenOn": "2015-11-02T20:47:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What if another power signal toggles at approximately the same time as your \"1 ms every 8s\" pulse? Then, you\u0027ll sample the periodic pulse, and maybe make a wrong conclusion about the actual power state?",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "765c8636_103505d4",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 510,
      "author": {
        "id": 1127214
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-03T00:49:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This periodic SLP_S0 pulse occurs only when S0ix state where SLP_S0 is asserted, unlike SLP_S3 which stays low when asserted.(this is due to unused PECI bus pin is grounded.).\nWhen SLP_S0 is de-asserted, there will be no more pulses.\n\nWhen other signals(SLP_S3 or S4) to be asserted, SLP_S0 is already de-asserted and it is unlikely for simultaneous signal changes.    \nAll these signal behaviour are controlled by PCH in SOC.",
      "parentUuid": "36204e91_546c85a0",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7643a650_5d72762f",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 510,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-03T18:36:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, it\u0027s not just a power signal toggle that can lead to misidentification of power state. Anything that wakes TASK_ID_CHIPSET can also cause it, right?\n\nMy suggestion is to create a variable that represents the debounced signal. The chipset task will deal with that variable only. Your ISR / deferred routine will deal with the actual signal and toggle the variable and wake the CHIPSET task when necessary.\n\nWe may need to introduce the concept of a power signal that\u0027s not actually a GPIO.",
      "parentUuid": "765c8636_103505d4",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b69d1e72_54c0824f",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 510,
      "author": {
        "id": 1127214
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-04T21:08:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just waking CHIPSET_TASK won\u0027t change power state unless \u0027power_update_signals()\u0027 is called.  Instead of power state, indirectly reading gpio(SLP_S) from power_update_signals() can give condition for waking CHIPSET_TASK.( please see next patch). \nRegarding your suggestion for variable, do you mean the variable indicate interrupt is valid(not pulse)? \nWhat do you expect to do in chipset task with this variable ?",
      "parentUuid": "7643a650_5d72762f",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b69d1e72_f706d89e",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 510,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-05T01:54:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, you are right. I still think we shouldn\u0027t be sampling the actual GPIO during the debounce period. I checked the code closer. Here is my proposal:\n\n-\u003e In gpio.h add a new flag GPIO_PS_DEBOUNCE to denote a power signal that must be debounced. It will be set for the SLP_S0 signal in gpio.inc.\n\n-\u003e In power_update_signals(), before calling gpio_get_level(), it will check for the GPIO_PS_DEBOUNCE flag. If set, instead of calling gpio_get_level() directly, it will call chipset_get_ps_debounced_level(s-\u003egpio). \n\n-\u003e chipset_get_ps_debounced_level() will be implemented in skylake.c - it should be easy to keep track of the debounced level of our GPIO with our deferred routine.\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "b69d1e72_54c0824f",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "36892e3b_36277ef7",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 510,
      "author": {
        "id": 1127214
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-05T03:34:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. I think you want to use \u0027power_signal_interrupt\u0027 instead of \u0027power_signal_interrupt_s0(), do you ? \n\n2. For implementing \"chipset_get_ps_debounced_level()\", can you explain more detail ?  we have \u0027in_signals\u0027 inside power_update_signals() to keep track of signal. Why don\u0027t we use this value before/after interrupt ?",
      "parentUuid": "b69d1e72_f706d89e",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f6923665_5f9b3b97",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 510,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-05T18:31:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "chipset_get_ps_debounced_level(gpio) will return the debounced state of the GPIO. For example, if you want to ignore 1ms pulses on a certain GPIO, you can record the last observed state of the GPIO and a timestamp in your ISR. chipset_get_ps_debounced_level() will return asserted / non-asserted based on the current GPIO state / current time and the previous observed GPIO state / previous time. For example, if the GPIO was last asserted 500us ago and  chipset_get_ps_debounced_level() is called, it should return non-asserted. On the other hand, if the GPIO was last asserted 1500us ago (and is still asserted), it should return asserted. This way, in_signals will reflect the debounced state of the GPIO (not the actual pin state) so you don\u0027t have to worry about the edge case we discussed above.",
      "parentUuid": "36892e3b_36277ef7",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "96a49abb_1f4e0f18",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 510,
      "author": {
        "id": 1127214
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-05T20:43:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "SLP_S0      1msec pulse\n___          ____\n   |________|    |_______\n     1      2 3  5    4\n\nWe want to ignore this 1 msec pulse.\n\na. in position 1(before interrupt), we know status from \u0027in_signals\u0027 via get_power_signals() in previous interrupt.\nb. in poistion 2, interrupt happens.\nc. in position 3, do you want to record pin status at \u00271\u0027 ?\nor at \u00273\u0027? \nd. \u0027chipset_get_ps_debounce_level() is called at \u00273\u0027 but can return result at \u00274\u0027. to judge if de-bounced or not can be done only by reading GPIO pin status.  \nHow chipset_get_ps_debounce_level() returns result ?\nDo you want delay inside interrupt to get result at 4 ? or deferred by hook ?\ne. Do you think interrupt at 5 should be serviced ?  \n\n\n\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\nHere is my implementation in patch 7:\nSLP_S0      _\n___________| |_______\n   1       2 4      3\n\na. in position 1(before interrupt), we know status from \u0027in_signals\u0027 via get_power_signals();.\nb. in poistion 2, interrupt happens. disable interrupt teporarily and interrupt at 4 will be ignored.\nc. in position 3, deferred task gets SLP_S0 status from power_update_signals(). re-enable interrupt. \nif (@1 \u003d\u003d @3), interrrupt at 2 is invalid and ignored.\nif (@1 !\u003d @3), interrupt at 2 is valid and wakeup chipset task.\nPlease see patch 7.",
      "parentUuid": "f6923665_5f9b3b97",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "765c8636_5c039925",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 515,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-02T20:47:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The purpose of these two functions is to debounce the 1ms pulse every 8s, right? Do you really need a separate ISR to do this? For example, why not call your deferred routine from _power_handle_state? In any case, it\u0027s probably best to put this code in skylake.c, not here.",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5625c29e_fd68183b",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 515,
      "author": {
        "id": 1127214
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-03T00:49:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The purpose of debounce is not to wakeup chipset task when interrupt is not valid since chipset task produces messages(\"power state S0ix \u003d 0x1d...\") and this message prevents idles task from entering heavy sleep.( need at least 1 min quiet/no UART activity).\n\"_power_handle_state\" is called only when chipset tast wakes up. \n\nTo move S0 interrupt and its deferred call to skylake.c, \"power_update_signal()\" should be NOT \u0027static\u0027 inside common.c and defined in header file. Do you think if this change is OK to move S0 interrupt to skyale?",
      "parentUuid": "765c8636_5c039925",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "765c8636_a98db4e5",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 515,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-03T18:36:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this S0ix code going to apply to future chipsets, or is the implementation here mostly skylake-specific (especially the 1ms pulse every 8s)? If it\u0027s the second case then definitely we don\u0027t want the code in power/common.c. If it\u0027s the first case, maybe it makes sense to put the code here (or a new file power/s0ix.c maybe).\n\nI don\u0027t think we want to make power_update_signals non-static.",
      "parentUuid": "5625c29e_fd68183b",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
